✅ REQUIRED (MUST-HAVE) RECORDS FOR CPANEL EMAIL



1️⃣ MX record (MOST IMPORTANT)
Type: MX
Host: @
Points to: mail.dlbwebservice.com
Priority: 0


✔ Tells the world where to deliver your email
✔ You already have this — correct

2️⃣ Mail server A record
Type: A
Host: mail
Points to: 185.195.12.114


✔ The MX record must point to something that resolves
✔ Required

3️⃣ SPF (anti-spam, REQUIRED)
Type: TXT
Host: @
Value: v=spf1 a mx ip4:185.195.12.114 ~all


✔ Prevents spam / improves delivery
✔ Correct

4️⃣ DKIM (email authentication)
Type: TXT
Host: default._domainkey
Value: v=DKIM1; k=rsa; p=...


✔ Cryptographically signs outgoing mail
✔ Auto-generated by cPanel
✔ Correct

5️⃣ DMARC (policy + reputation)
Type: TXT
Host: _dmarc
Value: v=DMARC1; p=none


✔ Controls how receivers handle failures
✔ Correct (you can tighten later)

✅ REQUIRED FOR WEBMAIL & LOGIN (NORMAL)

